    {
      "ordinal": 5,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "1.2",
      "title": "Sabatons description",
      "body": "Sabatons can be:\n● Plate sabatons : Made of metal plates riveted together, it is the most effective and the most common foot protection over all middle ages.\n● Brigand sabatons : Made of metal plates riveted to a leather base. This protection is not commonly represented in historical sources. The plates are covered by the leather.\n● Scales sabatons : Made of small scales riveted upon a leather base. This protection is not commonly represented in historical sources.\n● Chainmail sabatons : The protection of the foot is ensured by chainmail. This is the earliest foot protection documented by historical sources.\n● Eastern sabatons : Due to very few historical sources, we allow eastern stylization of European sabatons. Allowed designs are displayed in the document “Eastern Armors”.",
      "page_from": 3,
      "page_to": 3,
      "stable_key": "sabatons:1.2",
