    {
      "ordinal": 20,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "5.1",
      "title": "Historical sources and datation",
      "body": "● Chainmail sabatons are the earliest foot protection. They were popular in the XIIIth and early 14th century, and were replaced by more protective sabatons around the middle of the 14th century. They are still in use in very rare cases during the 15th century.\n● They are approved for 14th century armors and Transitional.\n● They are approved for 15th century armors if documented by sources. We encourage you to send an email to the authenticity committee before purchasing such sabatons and armors.\n● Their construction makes chainmail sabatons less protective than plate sabatons.\nTherefore, we do not recommend such sabatons in any category.\n\nPfarr- und Klosterkirche Sankt Lampert, Seeon-Seebruck, Bavaria - 1395 - Germany",
      "page_from": 11,
      "page_to": 11,
